abstract: >-
  Working Draft 0.6.1. A public working draft of requirements and a
  conformance reporting framework for advisory AI systems that answer from
  bounded, declared corpora of institutional texts. It distinguishes
  normative, interpretive and epistemic authority, defines four assurance
  layers, requires a published coverage statement, and states seventeen
  requirements, reported per requirement and property with no aggregate
  score. The requirements were abstracted from one procedural corpus (the
  Standing Orders and Speakers' Rulings of the New Zealand House of
  Representatives); application to other bounded institutional rule systems
  is intended, and application to legislation, case law and mixed legal
  research is not demonstrated. Several requirements are provisional, so no
  overall conformance claim is currently available. Formerly numbered KNIT
  RFC-0000. Not a standard; not an IETF RFC; not peer reviewed.
